  "digest": "# TECHNOLOGY \u2014 sector digest, ISO week 2026-W45\n\n**Coverage changes.** DCII.JK (DATA_CENTRES) is the desk's only published name: initiation v1, SELL, target Rp87,286 against a Rp174,975 price, expected total return -50.1% [coverage:DCII.JK; [report](companies/DCII.JK/report.md)]. No rating or target moved this week, and the price held at Rp174,975 into 6 Nov [price marks]. The pipeline widened instead: 46 technology initiations were queued on 5 Nov across INTERNET_PLATFORMS, SOFTWARE_IT_SERVICES, DATA_CENTRES and TECH_HARDWARE [fund record].\n\n**Deck moves.** All four technology industries read only the macro deck [operating configuration]; the desk has no industry deck of its own, and no deck value was re-sourced this week. The gaps that matter for these models are macro: USD/IDR spot 18,003.5 (6 Nov) against FY2027E 18,350 (-1.9%), BI rate 5.75% and CPI 3.28% both at forecast \u2014 nothing beyond the 15% drift threshold [deck:macro].\n\n**Material news.** DCII left the IHSG calculation on 2 Nov under the HSC reclassification [news triage 2026-11-01]. Among queued names: GOTO posted a third consecutive quarterly profit (Q3 net profit Rp441bn versus a Rp255bn loss, revenue +17% to Rp5.6trn), then cancelled its treasury shares and buyback; digital tax collection by banks, fintechs, GOTO and Lazada starts 9 Nov [2026-11-04/05, 2026-11-02]. CYBR grew gross profit 57% on Rp92.8bn revenue [2026-11-04]. Two technology names, LMAS and ENVY, are among the 18 issuers delisted on 10 Nov; MENN is suspended for not filing; KIOS appears on OJK's 2026 sanctions list [2026-11-04/05, 2026-11-01].\n\n**What to watch.** The 10 Nov delistings and the 9 Nov tax start; GOTO's initiation and whether its profit streak survives the levy; DCII's dated 31 Mar 2027 free-float step; and a macro-deck provenance check \u2014 the USD/IDR spot carries a Yahoo IDR=X print (18,003.5) that the deck's own basis rejects in favour of the Rp18,080 onshore close of 23 Oct [deck:macro].\n\n*Research only; not a recommendation to act.*",
  "digest_file": "fund record"
